{"event":"step_update","step_update":{"conversation_id":"7c9d0750-b424-4a04-846f-f3a104d74b44","step_index":215,"state":"DONE","step_type":"agent_response","text_delta":"The Intervals.icu OAuth integration has been fixed, and the root causes have been documented in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-izGZ62/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary of Causes \u0026 Fixes\n\n1. **Connect Button 401 Unauthorized for All Athletes**\n   - **Cause**: The \"Connect Intervals.icu\" button was a direct link (`\u003ca href=\"/api/intervals/auth/init\"\u003e`). Normal browser document navigation does not attach the `Authorization: Bearer \u003ctoken\u003e` stored in `localStorage`, causing `require_user()` to reject the request with `401 Unauthorized`.\n   - **Fix**: Added `POST /api/intervals/auth/init` support in [server.py](file:///tmp/h-izGZ62/server.py#L149-L171) to return the authorization URL as JSON (`{ \"authorize_url\": ... }`), and updated [static/app.js](file:///tmp/h-izGZ62/static/app.js#L26-L45) to call it using the authenticated `api()` fetch wrapper before redirecting via `window.location.assign(res.authorize_url)`.\n\n2. **Authorization Link Failing with 400 `invalid_request` (`Duplicate scope`)**\n   - **Cause**: In [config.py](file:///tmp/h-izGZ62/config.py), the `SCOPES` string specified both read and write scopes for the same areas (`ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE...CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE`). Because Intervals.icu's `:WRITE` scopes implicitly grant read access, specifying both triggered Intervals.icu's strict `Duplicate scope` validation rejection.\n   - **Fix**: Updated `SCOPES` in [config.py](file:///tmp/h-izGZ62/config.py#L11) to specify each permission area once with the highest privilege needed: `\"ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE\"`.\n\n3. **Premature Disconnection After 1 Hour (\"Status: expired, reconnect\")**\n   - **Cause**: Intervals.icu OAuth access tokens are perpetual and do not return `refresh_token` or `expires_in`. The server defaulted missing expiration times to 3600 seconds and ran a background `refresh_tokens()` thread. When the hour elapsed without a refresh token, the worker forcibly demoted connected accounts to `\"expired, reconnect\"`.\n   - **Fix**:\n     - Removed the synthetic 1-hour expiration and the background refresh thread in [server.py](file:///tmp/h-izGZ62/server.py).\n     - Streamlined `exchange_code()` to post only `client_id`, `client_secret`, and `code`.\n     - Switched to lazy token invalidation handling: when an athlete revokes access, any subsequent 401 from Intervals.icu updates their status to `\"expired, reconnect\"`.\n","duration_seconds":9.344708,"usage":{"input_tokens":2283,"output_tokens":651,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":113044,"total_tokens":2934}}}
{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"7c9d0750-b424-4a04-846f-f3a104d74b44","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The Intervals.icu OAuth integration has been fixed, and the root causes have been documented in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-izGZ62/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary of Causes \u0026 Fixes\n\n1. **Connect Button 401 Unauthorized for All Athletes**\n   - **Cause**: The \"Connect Intervals.icu\" button was a direct link (`\u003ca href=\"/api/intervals/auth/init\"\u003e`). Normal browser document navigation does not attach the `Authorization: Bearer \u003ctoken\u003e` stored in `localStorage`, causing `require_user()` to reject the request with `401 Unauthorized`.\n   - **Fix**: Added `POST /api/intervals/auth/init` support in [server.py](file:///tmp/h-izGZ62/server.py#L149-L171) to return the authorization URL as JSON (`{ \"authorize_url\": ... }`), and updated [static/app.js](file:///tmp/h-izGZ62/static/app.js#L26-L45) to call it using the authenticated `api()` fetch wrapper before redirecting via `window.location.assign(res.authorize_url)`.\n\n2. **Authorization Link Failing with 400 `invalid_request` (`Duplicate scope`)**\n   - **Cause**: In [config.py](file:///tmp/h-izGZ62/config.py), the `SCOPES` string specified both read and write scopes for the same areas (`ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE...CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE`). Because Intervals.icu's `:WRITE` scopes implicitly grant read access, specifying both triggered Intervals.icu's strict `Duplicate scope` validation rejection.\n   - **Fix**: Updated `SCOPES` in [config.py](file:///tmp/h-izGZ62/config.py#L11) to specify each permission area once with the highest privilege needed: `\"ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE\"`.\n\n3. **Premature Disconnection After 1 Hour (\"Status: expired, reconnect\")**\n   - **Cause**: Intervals.icu OAuth access tokens are perpetual and do not return `refresh_token` or `expires_in`. The server defaulted missing expiration times to 3600 seconds and ran a background `refresh_tokens()` thread. When the hour elapsed without a refresh token, the worker forcibly demoted connected accounts to `\"expired, reconnect\"`.\n   - **Fix**:\n     - Removed the synthetic 1-hour expiration and the background refresh thread in [server.py](file:///tmp/h-izGZ62/server.py).\n     - Streamlined `exchange_code()` to post only `client_id`, `client_secret`, and `code`.\n     - Switched to lazy token invalidation handling: when an athlete revokes access, any subsequent 401 from Intervals.icu updates their status to `\"expired, reconnect\"`.\n","duration_seconds":614.068401,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":328432,"output_tokens":11205,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":6790603,"total_tokens":339637}}}
